Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:35:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(chat): compact panel chrome + closed-state pill

The panel spent ~104px on chrome before the conversation: a 48px grabber
row stacked on a ~56px bar that held a 24px wordmark and four floating
icons. On a phone that is 12% of the screen for two controls' worth of
meaning.

- the grabber moves inside the bar (26x4, 48px hit area); the bar itself
  becomes the sheet's drag surface, so the separate row is gone
- bar is 48px (52px on mobile, safe-area padded) instead of ~104px total
- the wordmark shrinks to 18px/16px and a hairline + 'Chat with me' label
  fills the space that was empty
- the four actions read as one bordered cluster: 32px buttons, 44px
  pointer targets, 2px gaps
- new closed-state pill (bottom right) so the assistant is one tap away
  instead of existing only while the sheet is open

Behaviour is unchanged: same detents, keyboard avoidance, focus trap,
drag-resize on desktop, skeleton, retry and announcements. The header
drag ignores presses that start on a button and is disabled above 900px,
where resizing happens from the left edge.
